---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Src from '../components/Src.astro';
import Aff from '../components/Aff.astro';
import Unverified from '../components/Unverified.astro';
import { S } from '../data/sources.js';
const title = 'The Cheapest Virtual Mailbox in 2026 (and When It Stops Being Cheap)';
const description = 'The lowest advertised virtual mailbox prices: Anytime Mailbox from $4.99, PostScan Mail from $8.33 a month billed annually, iPostal1 from $9.99, Traveling Mailbox $15 with scans included. Which one is cheapest depends on how much mail you open.';
const schema = {"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Article","headline":title,"description":description,"dateModified":"2026-11-19"};
---
<Base title={title} description={description} schema={schema}>
  <h1>The cheapest virtual mailbox</h1>
  <p class="lede">The lowest advertised price is Anytime Mailbox: "Our cheapest virtual mailbox plans are $4.99" <Src href={S.atm} />. But the cheapest plan only stays cheapest if you rarely open mail. Prices below were checked on November 19, 2026.</p>

  <h2>Lowest advertised prices</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Rank</th><th>Provider</th><th>Lowest advertised price</th><th>The catch</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>1</td><td>Anytime Mailbox</td><td>$4.99; "on average, our plans cost $9.99 per month" <Src href={S.atm} /></td><td>Each location sets its own plans and fees, so the $4.99 address may not be in your city <Src href={S.atm} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>2</td><td>PostScan Mail</td><td>$8.33/mo Starter, billed annually; "as low as $10/mo" monthly <Src href={S.psm} /></td><td>No free open-and-scans on Starter. Each one is $2.00 for up to 10 pages, and junk mail counts toward your 30-item limit <Src href={S.psm} /> <Src href={S.psmFaq} label="FAQ" /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>3</td><td>iPostal1</td><td>From $9.99/mo (Virtual Mailing Address) <Src href={S.ip} /></td><td>Plan allowances vary by location <Unverified />. The online notary for Form 1583 is $25 unless your mail center lets you sign in person <Src href={S.ipFaq} /></td></tr>
      <tr><td>4</td><td>Traveling Mailbox</td><td>$15/mo Basic <Src href={S.tmb} /></td><td>Highest sticker price of the four, but 35 page scans a month are included, and Form 1583 needs no notary <Src href={S.tmb} /> <Src href={S.tmbKb} label="1583" /></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2>Cheapest for your situation</h2>
  <div class="cards">
    <div class="card"><h3>You just need an address</h3><p>An Anytime Mailbox or iPostal1 location is cheapest when you mostly recycle mail and only look at envelope images.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>You open 5+ letters a month</h3><p>Traveling Mailbox Basic includes 35 page scans for $15 <Src href={S.tmb} />. At PostScan, five open-and-scans on Starter add $10 to the bill <Src href={S.psm} />.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>You want to skip the notary</h3><p>Traveling Mailbox, Stable and US Global Mail handle Form 1583 without a notary <Src href={S.tmbKb} /> <Src href={S.stable1583} /> <Src href={S.usgm1583} />. That saves the $20–$25 online notary fee charged elsewhere <Src href={S.psmFaq} /> <Src href={S.ipFaq} />.</p></div>
  </div>

  <h2>Don't forget the setup cost</h2>
  <p>Some providers require a notarized USPS Form 1583 before they'll handle your mail. iPostal1's online notary costs $25 <Src href={S.ipFaq} /> and PostScan's partner notary costs $20 <Src href={S.psmFaq} />. Over a year on a $9.99 plan, a $25 notary fee adds about 20%. See <a href="/usps-form-1583-online-notarization/">Form 1583 and online notarization</a>.</p>

  <h2>Links</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><Aff id="anytimemailbox" href="https://www.anytimemailbox.com/" text="Anytime Mailbox locations" /></li>
    <li><Aff id="postscanmail" href="https://www.postscanmail.com/" text="PostScan Mail" /></li>
    <li><Aff id="ipostal1" href="https://ipostal1.com/" text="iPostal1" /></li>
    <li><Aff id="travelingmailbox" href="https://www.travelingmailbox.com/" text="Traveling Mailbox" /></li>
  </ul>
  <p>Full table: <a href="/virtual-mailbox-pricing-comparison/">virtual mailbox pricing compared</a>.</p>
</Base>
